<%# Standing status disclosure. Fuime shows balances, ledgers and cards, which is
    exactly the presentation that invites a reader to assume a bank and deposit
    insurance sit behind it. 12 CFR 328.102(b)(3)(ii) treats omitting the
    information needed to prevent that assumption as the violation, so this is
    stated unconditionally rather than only on money-related pages, and it is in
    the always-visible block for the same reason the legal links are.
    When a partner bank exists, this becomes the "banking services provided by
    [Bank], Member FDIC" form — until then, naming a bank here would itself be
    the false claim. %>
<%# The entity is named here and not only in the terms because this is the
    disclosure a reader sees without clicking anything, and "Fuime is a
    financial technology company" invited the reading that Fuime IS the
    company. It is a product; the company is the one that would answer for it. %>
<%# Extracted from application/_footer so layouts that set `no_app_shell` — which
    never render that footer — can carry the same sentence. The family setup
    wizard is one: eight pages where somebody signs a legal agreement, and the
    footer this text used to live in does not render on any of them. The bytes
    are unchanged; spec/requests/fuime/status_disclosure_spec.rb matches on
    them. %>
<p class="text-xs text-center mx-auto" style="max-width: 44rem;">
  Fuime is a product of <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>,
  a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not hold
  deposits and does not offer FDIC-insured products. Payments are processed by
  Stripe. <%= fuime_footer_ownership %>
</p>
